<metadata><name>Day 14 - Norman Pearson, Eric Best, King, McNally, Smokey Hollow</name></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.330803" lon="-79.886980"><name>P Start/finish parking</name><desc>Great Falls: Parking area beside Mill St, at the Smokey Hollow Side Trail. Free</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.337990" lon="-79.865820"><name>P2 alternative parking</name><desc>Roadside parking on King Rd. Free. Joins the route near km 4.3 (0 m walk).</desc><sym>Parking Area</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.330472" lon="-79.886672"><name>J1</name><desc>J1: Continue straight onto the white-blazed main Bruce Trail, heading south-east. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off on your left.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.324816" lon="-79.885666"><name>J2</name><desc>J2: Turn left onto the blue-blazed Norman Pearson Side Trail, heading east. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off ahead.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.329028" lon="-79.878003"><name>J3</name><desc>J3: Continue straight onto the blue-blazed McNally Side Trail, heading east. (the blue-blazed McNally Side Trail goes off on your left.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.329389" lon="-79.876269"><name>J4</name><desc>J4: End of the McNally Side Trail. Turn around and retrace your steps.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.331450" lon="-79.879895"><name>J5</name><desc>J5: Turn right onto the white-blazed main Bruce Trail, heading east. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off ahead.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.341903" lon="-79.862418"><name>J6</name><desc>J6: Turn left onto the blue-blazed King Side Trail, heading north. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off ahead.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.341913" lon="-79.865219"><name>J7</name><desc>J7: Turnaround point. Turn around and retrace your steps.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.332310" lon="-79.884011"><name>J8</name><desc>J8: Turn right onto the blue-blazed Eric Best Side Trail, heading south. (the white-blazed main Bruce Trail goes off on your left.)</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.332747" lon="-79.886359"><name>J9</name><desc>J9: Start the Eric Best Side Trail loop (0.6 km). Continue straight onto it, heading north-east; it brings you back to this junction.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
